Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Skip empty lock screen; instead go straight to password entry.
;
; NOTE: this may cause Windows to block the user from changing their lock
; screen background in the settings menu.  If so, this can be undone with the
; lock-screen-enable.reg file.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Personalization]
"NoLockScreen"=dword:00000001
